WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.394
King Jolliginki and Queen Ermintrude lived deep in the jungle.

2
00:00:05.395 --> 00:00:08.178
Dr. Dolittle now stood before them.

3
00:00:08.179 --> 00:00:12.298
"What is your business here?" King Jolliginki roared.

4
00:00:12.299 --> 00:00:15.517
His voice was much louder than that of most men.

5
00:00:15.518 --> 00:00:19.035
That’s why it sounded like a roar.

6
00:00:19.036 --> 00:00:22.595
Dr. Dolittle explained why he came to Africa.

7
00:00:22.596 --> 00:00:25.290
The king listened carefully.

8
00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:32.042
"May I travel through your land to help the monkeys?" the doctor asked politely.

9
00:00:32.043 --> 00:00:34.887
"No!" the king shook his head.

10
00:00:34.888 --> 00:00:37.569
Dr. Dolittle could not believe his ears.

11
00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:42.084
"Why not, your Majesty?" he asked.

12
00:00:42.085 --> 00:00:44.779
"Many years ago," replied the king.

13
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.015
"I allowed a man to go through my land.

14
00:00:48.016 --> 00:00:51.710
I was kind to him, but do you know what he did?

15
00:00:51.711 --> 00:00:58.074
He killed my elephants, dug up my gold, and chopped down my trees!

16
00:00:58.075 --> 00:01:03.183
I will never again let a stranger go through my land. NEVER!"

17
00:01:03.184 --> 00:01:06.074
King Jolliginki turned to his guards.

18
00:01:06.075 --> 00:01:08.585
"To the dungeon!" he ordered.

19
00:01:08.586 --> 00:01:13.322
Dr. Dolittle and the animals were dragged away to the dungeon.

20
00:01:13.323 --> 00:01:17.216
It was cold, dirty, and dark in the dungeon.

21
00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:21.153
"I wish we had never come here," cried Gub-Gub.

22
00:01:21.154 --> 00:01:23.591
Then he started to cry.

23
00:01:23.592 --> 00:01:28.038
"Be quiet or else I’ll hit you!" Chee-Chee warned.

24
00:01:28.039 --> 00:01:34.561
"Dr. Dolittle! Dr. Dolittle!" The animals surrounded him.

25
00:01:34.562 --> 00:01:38.261
"Is everyone here?" Dr. Dolittle blinked.

26
00:01:38.262 --> 00:01:43.661
"No. We can’t find Polynesia," Jip replied sadly.

27
00:01:43.662 --> 00:01:48.408
"Oh, no! Polynesia! Polynesia!"

28
00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:52.494
Dr. Dolittle looked around for his beloved bird.

29
00:01:52.495 --> 00:01:57.143
"SSSSH! I’m here!" whispered a voice from the window.

30
00:01:57.144 --> 00:01:58.600
They all looked up.

31
00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:02.745
"POLYNESIA!" they shouted.

32
00:02:02.746 --> 00:02:08.640
"SHHHHHHH! Quiet! The guards will hear you!" Polynesia whispered.

33
00:02:08.641 --> 00:02:13.953
"You must get us out of here, Polynesia," Dr. Dolittle pleaded.

34
00:02:13.954 --> 00:02:18.218
"Don’t worry, Dr. Dolittle," Polynesia comforted him,

35
00:02:18.219 --> 00:02:20.175
"I already have a plan."

36
00:02:20.176 --> 00:02:27.534
"YIPPPIE! Polynesia will get us out!" shouted Gub-Gub.

37
00:02:27.535 --> 00:02:31.588
That night, Polynesia flew into the king’s bedroom.

38
00:02:31.589 --> 00:02:34.613
She pretended to be Dr. Dolittle.

39
00:02:34.614 --> 00:02:39.018
"King Jolliginki!" Polynesia said in the doctor’s voice.

40
00:02:39.019 --> 00:02:42.493
"Huh? Ermintrude, is that you?"

41
00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:45.123
The king thought it was the queen.

42
00:02:45.124 --> 00:02:49.649
"King Jolliginki!" the bird called out, more loudly.

43
00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:56.013
"Who’s there? Show yourself!" King Jolliginki said.

44
00:02:56.014 --> 00:03:00.830
"I am the great Dr. Dolittle!" Polynesia replied.

45
00:03:00.831 --> 00:03:05.268
"Show yourself!" repeated the terrified king.

46
00:03:05.269 --> 00:03:10.996
"Listen to me, foolish king," Polynesia said in a low voice.

47
00:03:10.997 --> 00:03:14.787
King Jolliginki was getting very scared.

48
00:03:14.788 --> 00:03:16.699
"You are in my dungeon!

49
00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:20.398
How can you speak to me?" he cried.

50
00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:22.395
"Of course you cannot see me.

51
00:03:22.396 --> 00:03:26.089
I am invisible," Polynesia laughed.

52
00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:29.098
"No, that’s impossible!"

53
00:03:29.099 --> 00:03:32.038
His voice sounded squeaky and high.

54
00:03:32.039 --> 00:03:35.431
"Let us go!" Polynesia commanded.

55
00:03:35.432 --> 00:03:39.854
"NO! I can’t!" the king sobbed.

56
00:03:39.855 --> 00:03:44.409
"If you don’t, then I will make you sick like the monkeys!"

57
00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:50.498
"Who is the king talking to?" wondered Queen Ermintrude.

58
00:03:50.499 --> 00:03:53.181
The king did not want to suffer.

59
00:03:53.182 --> 00:03:57.786
"Guards! Guards! Release the prisoners!" he roared.

60
00:03:57.787 --> 00:04:00.680
The guards ran toward the dungeon.

61
00:04:00.681 --> 00:04:03.720
Polynesia flew out the window.

62
00:04:03.721 --> 00:04:08.279
At that moment, Queen Ermintrude turned and saw her.

63
00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.852
"What is that parrot doing here?"

64
00:04:10.853 --> 00:04:14.117
she asked her puzzled husband.

65
00:04:14.118 --> 00:04:17.333
Polynesia had no time to waste.

66
00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:22.038
"Dr. Dolittle! Wake up! Get ready!" she gasped.

67
00:04:22.039 --> 00:04:26.580
Before the doctor could answer, the guards opened the door.

68
00:04:26.581 --> 00:04:31.466
"By the king’s orders, you are free to go!" shouted a guard.

69
00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:34.252
"Quickly! Doctor! Follow me!"

70
00:04:34.253 --> 00:04:38.166
Polynesia said in the animal language.

71
00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:41.856
"Stop! Stop! Don’t let the prisoners go!"

72
00:04:41.857 --> 00:04:44.520
The king ran toward the dungeon.

73
00:04:44.522 --> 00:04:47.033
The king now knew he had been tricked.

74
00:04:47.034 --> 00:04:51.861
"It was the parrot pretending to be the doctor," his wife had said.

75
00:04:51.862 --> 00:04:53.750
But it was too late.

76
00:04:53.751 --> 00:04:59.511
The doctor and all his animals were gone.

